  partName: Blade11
  description: The Blade11 is a tiny, elongated blade located at the middle-center-center
    of the jet engine, made of Blades texture material, tasked with channeling and
    accelerating the air through the engine, with a notable feature being its textured
    surface that reduces turbulence and enhances airflow. Its elongated shape provides
    a larger surface area, allowing for more efficient energy transfer, and its position
    in the compressor stage makes it crucial for the engine's overall performance.
    By optimizing airflow and minimizing losses, Blade11 contributes to the engine's
    ability to produce high thrust levels.
